From 60f03353f080d0ae62d3b7e422094c199fec6f58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corpus review <review@local>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 00:43:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Batch 2: pointer coverage for teeth, skull, vulva,
 shoulder, cord and airway

- part-pins.js: +47 pointers (dentition 9, skull 6, vulva 3, shoulder 12,
  spinal cord 8, upper airway/larynx 20) using the same dot + hairline +
  label system as the rest of the atlas.
- New second-plate mechanism (app.js partPlate): structures hidden on the
  chapter plate can carry their own pin on another shipped plate, e.g. the
  medial skull view for sphenoid/ethmoid/vomer/palate, and the clitoral
  complex plate for crura, vestibular bulbs and pudendal branches. 16 parts.
- miniChip(): a lens row without its own micro-point stays an honest
  reference chip (data-preview-context=true), so previews never claim a
  location for a tissue-type image.
- build_seo.py: ship part-pins.js in the build, and stop repeating the
  foundations microscope gallery as lens tiles (fixes the two duplicate
  tissue entries and the SEO audit).
- index.html: cache-bust v=50.

Coverage: 967 pinned + 16 second-plate + 194 lens = 74.2% of 1,586 parts
(was 40.7% before this work). 0 label overlaps and 0 broken images across
all 74 chapters. SEO audit PASS (79 pages).
